<title>UK: Ex-dividends take 5.53 points off FTSE, June 2.</title>
<headline>Ex-dividends take 5.53 points off FTSE, June 2.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following FTSE-100 stocks go ex-dividend on Monday and have taken 5.53 points off the index at the start of trading.</p>
<p>							DIVIDEND	 INDEX</p>
<p>							(PENCE)	  EFFECT</p>
<p>	   COMPANY				 Net   Gross     Gross</p>
<p> * Bass PLC					8.30  10.375    0.536</p>
<p> * British Airways			    10.80  13.500    0.790</p>
<p> * LucasVarity				   2.25   2.813    0.233</p>
<p> * Imperial Tobacco			    7.20   9.000    0.274</p>
<p> * Land Securities			    19.65  24.563    0.741</p>
<p> * Mercury Asset Management		 35.00  43.750    0.467</p>
<p> * National Power			     19.00  23.750    1.681</p>
<p> * PowerGen				     17.40  21.750    0.808</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
